From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <spolack+claude@mailbox.org>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 10:31:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] network: do not fail setup when the interface has no ifindex

net->ifindex is consumed only by the VXLAN service. Requiring it unnecessarily
excludes platforms where the WireGuard device has no netdev name resolvable by
if_nametoindex(), such as a tun created by an Android VpnService. Keep the hard
failure when VXLAN support is compiled in, and warn otherwise.
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PVGaNeNhqp11rTLwZ9rM4J
---
 network.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/network.c b/network.c
index fd776ac..2844b39 100644
--- a/network.c
+++ b/network.c
@@ -611,8 +611,17 @@ static int network_setup(struct network *net)
 
 	net->ifindex = if_nametoindex(network_name(net));
 	if (!net->ifindex) {
+#ifdef VXLAN_SUPPORT
 		fprintf(stderr, "Could not get ifindex for network %s\n", network_name(net));
 		return -1;
+#else
+		/*
+		 * Only the VXLAN service consumes net->ifindex. Platforms where
+		 * the WireGuard device has no resolvable netdev name (e.g. an
+		 * Android VpnService tun) must still be able to set up a network.
+		 */
+		D_NET(net, "no ifindex for interface, continuing without it");
+#endif
 	}
 
 	return 0;
